{title: All Praise to Thee, My God, This Night}
{artist: Thomas Ken / Thomas Tallis}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: all-praise-to-thee-my-god-this-night.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (All_Praise_To_Thee_My_God_This_Night-Tallis_Canon) and the Cyber Hymnal score (91% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]All [D]praise to [Em]Thee, my [Am]God, [D]this [G]night,
[G]For [Am]all the [G]blessings [Am]of [D7]the [G]light!
[G]Keep [Am]me, O [G]keep me, [Am]King [D]of [G]kings,
[G]Be[Am]neath [D]Thine [Em]own al[Am]migh[D]ty [G]wings.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]For[D]give me, [Em]Lord, for [Am]Thy [D]dear [G]Son,
[G]The [Am]ill that [G]I this [Am]day [D7]have [G]done,
[G]That [Am]with the [G]world, my[Am]self, [D]and [G]Thee,
[G]I, [Am]ere [D]I [Em]sleep, at [Am]peace [D]may [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Teach [D]me to [Em]live, that [Am]I [D]may [G]dread
[G]The [Am]grave as [G]little [Am]as [D7]my [G]bed.
[G]Teach [Am]me to [G]die, that [Am]so [D]I [G]may
[G]Rise [Am]glo[D]rious [Em]at the [Am]judg[D]ment [G]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O [D]may my [Em]soul on [Am]Thee [D]re[G]pose,
[G]And [Am]with sweet [G]sleep mine [Am]eye[D7]lids [G]close,
[G]Sleep [Am]that may [G]me more [Am]vi[D]gorous [G]make
[G]To [Am]serve [D]my [Em]God when [Am]I [D]a[G]wake.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]When [D]in the [Em]night I [Am]sleep[D]less [G]lie,
[G]My [Am]soul with [G]heav’nly [Am]thoughts [D7]sup[G]ply;
[G]Let [Am]no ill [G]dreams dis[Am]turb [D]my [G]rest,
[G]No [Am]pow’rs [D]of [Em]darkness [Am]me [D]mo[G]lest.
{end_of_verse}
